From: Raven Developers <raven@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] endpoint: disable Nagle on outgoing TCP connections

Accepted TCP sockets already use TCP_NODELAY. Apply the same policy to
client sockets so small HIL actuator packets do not wait for delayed ACKs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Raven Developers <raven@localhost>
---
--- a/src/endpoint.cpp
+++ b/src/endpoint.cpp
@@ -1624,6 +1624,14 @@
         return false;
     }
 
+    // Match accepted sockets: flight-control packets must not wait for
+    // Nagle's algorithm on outgoing simulator or telemetry connections.
+    int tcp_nodelay_state = 1;
+    if (setsockopt(fd, IPPROTO_TCP, TCP_NODELAY, (char *)&tcp_nodelay_state, sizeof(int)) < 0) {
+        log_error("Error setting TCP_NODELAY on [%d]%s", fd, _name.c_str());
+        goto fail;
+    }
+
     // common setup
     if (connect(fd, sock, addrlen) < 0) {
         log_error("%d Error connecting to %s:%lu (%m)", fd, ip.c_str(), port);
